      "c-74a9c318c0c016cc": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-475",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "During the heat of the day the shepherds are in the habit of leading their flocks to some cool and shady spot, where they recline and rest until the shadows lengthen. The sheep sleep, or chew the cud, while the shepherds pass the time in some light employment, such as plaiting ma…",
